# 🧬 Project 01: Evolutionary Conservation of the Human TP53 Protein

## Project Overview

This project explores the evolutionary conservation of the **human TP53 protein** through comparative bioinformatics analysis. Using the human TP53 protein as the reference sequence, homologous proteins from different mammalian species are identified, aligned, and analyzed to infer their evolutionary relationships.

Participants will gain hands-on experience with sequence retrieval, homology searching, multiple sequence alignment, phylogenetic tree construction, and tree visualization using widely used bioinformatics tools.

---

# Project Objectives

* Retrieve the human TP53 protein sequence from the NCBI Protein database.
* Identify homologous TP53 proteins using BLASTp.
* Perform multiple sequence alignment using ClustalW in MEGA 12.
* Construct a Neighbor-Joining phylogenetic tree.
* Visualize and annotate the phylogenetic tree using iTOL.
* Interpret the evolutionary relationships among TP53 proteins.

---

